<article class="env-construction" id="0148">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0148">Construction <span data-tag="0148">3.6.5.1</span> <span class="named">(Geometric Realization as a Simplicial Functor)</span>.</a> Let $X$ and $Y$ be simplicial sets and let $\sigma $ be an $n$-simplex of the simplicial set $\operatorname{Fun}(X,Y)$, which we identify with a morphism $\Delta ^ n \times X \rightarrow Y$. By virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="013E" href="/tag/013E">3.6.2.2</a>, the geometric realization of $\sigma $ can be identified with a continuous function </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  |\sigma |: | \Delta ^{n} | \times |X| \rightarrow |Y|, \]
</div>
<p> which we can view as an $n$-simplex of the simplicial set $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Top}}(|X|,|Y|)_{\bullet }$ parametrizing continuous functions from $X$ to $Y$ (see Example <a data-tag="00JV" href="/tag/00JV">2.4.1.5</a>). This construction is compatible with face and degeneracy operators, and therefore determines a morphism of simplicial sets $\operatorname{Fun}(X,Y) \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Top}}( |X|, |Y| )_{\bullet }$. Allowing $X$ and $Y$ to vary, we obtain a simplicial structure on the geometric realization functor $| \bullet |: \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}\rightarrow \operatorname{Top}$. </p>
</article>
